#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1071
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1187
msgid "Temporary block"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1072
msgid "Network and CDN"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1073
#: includes/class-pncp-health.php:452
msgid "Blocking at the CDN"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1074
msgid "IP lists"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1084
msgid "Monitor only (log what would be blocked, block nothing)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1084
msgid "Every check below still runs, but a request it would refuse is let through and written to the log as “Would block”. No IP is blocked temporarily and nothing is blocked at the CDN. Use it to see what the settings would do before they do it: you and your staff are exempt, so you would never notice a block yourselves. Private URLs (feeds with a token) and Lockdown are not affected: they keep protecting."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: date and time
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1091
#, php-format
msgid "New install: ScrapeLock starts blocking on its own on %s. Untick the box (or use “Enforce now”) to start earlier; turned on by hand, “Monitor only” has no end."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1099
msgid "Who may read the site: the bot list, AI crawlers, and the User-Agents, IPs and referrers that are always allowed or always blocked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1100
msgid "Scrapers and bots"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1102
msgid "Block (403) the User-Agents in the list"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1103
msgid "Block requests without a User-Agent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1104
msgid "Block fake Googlebot, Bingbot, Applebot and Yandex"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1104
msgid "The IP is checked against the official Google and Bing lists and with reverse DNS. Real search engines always pass, without limits."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1105
msgid "Browsers only: 403 for pages without Accept-Language or without “Mozilla/” in the User-Agent"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1105
msgid "Stops most scripts. Link previews (Facebook, Viber, WhatsApp etc.) in the “Always allowed” list pass."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1106
msgid "Block headless and fake browsers"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1106
msgid "Blocks Chrome running without a window when it says so in its headers (“HeadlessChrome”), and, on HTTPS, scripts that copy the User-Agent of Chrome, Edge or Firefox without the Sec-Fetch headers every modern browser sends. It catches common tools and cheap scrapers, not every automated browser: one that is carefully disguised (e.g. Puppeteer with “stealth”, or Selenium with a visible Chrome) sends the same headers as a person. The page limits, the human check and the bot trap still apply to those. In-app browsers (Android WebView) are not checked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1107
#: includes/class-pncp-log.php:249
#: includes/class-pncp-status.php:450
msgid "Bot trap"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1107
msgid "Invisible link on every page, disallowed in robots.txt. Whoever opens it is blocked temporarily, even if it pretends to be a browser. Visitors do not see it, and another site cannot trap them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1108
msgid "User-Agents to block (one per line, matches anywhere in the User-Agent, case-insensitive):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1108
msgid "It contains two AI categories: training crawlers (GPTBot, ClaudeBot, CCBot, Google-Extended etc.) and AI search / assistants (OAI-SearchBot, ChatGPT-User, Claude-SearchBot, PerplexityBot etc.). You can allow the second one in the next section."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: number of AI crawlers
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1108
#, php-format
msgid "In addition, %s more AI crawlers and agents (DeepSeek, Grok, Qwen, Mistral, NotebookLM and others) are blocked by name: that list is built into ScrapeLock and updated with each version, so it is not shown here. A line that starts with “=” must be the whole User-Agent, e.g. “=node”."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: number of AI crawlers
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1109
msgid "Also block generic HTTP libraries (strict)"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: number of AI crawlers
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1109
msgid "Blocks the User-Agent that programming libraries send by default: curl, Wget, python-requests, Go, Java, okhttp, Dart, node-fetch, axios, Guzzle and others. Many cheap scrapers use them, but so do WooCommerce mobile apps (Flutter, Android), headless front ends, ERP and price sync, and uptime monitors. Turn it on only if nothing like that reads your site, or add those services to “Always allowed” first."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of User-Agents, e.g. "curl/, okhttp, Dart/"
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1117
#, php-format
msgid "Your bot list above still contains generic HTTP libraries (%s), so they are blocked even with this option off: lists saved before ScrapeLock 3.4 had them by default. If a mobile app, a headless front end or a sync service gets a 403, remove those lines from the list, or allow the service in “Always allowed”."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1125
msgid "AI search and training"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1127
msgid "Allow AI search engines and assistants (not training crawlers)"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of User-Agents
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1127
#, php-format
msgid "So the site appears in AI search answers with a link, without being given for model training. Allowed: %s. They are also removed from the robots.txt Disallow and from the server rules. The page limit still applies, because the User-Agent can be spoofed."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of User-Agents
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1128
msgid "Verify AI search bots with their official IP lists (OpenAI, Perplexity, Anthropic)"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of User-Agents
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1128
msgid "With AI search allowed: the real OAI-SearchBot, ChatGPT-User, PerplexityBot, Perplexity-User, Claude-SearchBot and Claude-User are never limited or blocked, and requests that only use their name get a 403 (“Fake AI search bot”). The lists are downloaded once a day; until then nothing changes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1129
msgid "Declare AI crawlers in robots.txt (Disallow)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1129
msgid "Applies to the virtual robots.txt of WordPress. If a physical robots.txt file exists, it takes precedence."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1130
msgid "Block web archives (Wayback Machine)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1130
msgid "The Internet Archive keeps a public copy of every page it visits, and that copy can be scraped without ever reaching your site. This blocks its crawlers (ia_archiver, archive.org_bot, heritrix) and asks them in robots.txt. Copies already in the archive stay there. Leave it off if you want your site to be archived."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1131
msgid "Content Signals in robots.txt: search yes, AI training no"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1131
msgid "A line that says what the content may be used for (contentsignals.org): search=yes, ai-train=no, and ai-input according to “Allow AI search engines”. It does not block anything; it is a statement of your terms that well-behaved companies read."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1136
msgid "Always allowed User-Agents (link previews, price comparison platforms, monitoring):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1136
msgid "They override the bot list and “Browsers only”. The page limit applies to them too, because the User-Agent is easy to spoof. To accept an entry only from specific IPs, add @ and the addresses, e.g. Skroutz@203.0.113.0/24."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1137
msgid "Always allowed IPs / CIDR (office, ERP, monitoring), one per line:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1137
msgid "They are never checked, never count towards limits and are never blocked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1142
msgid "IPs / CIDR that are always blocked (403), one per line:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1142
msgid "For example a scraper's server or a hosting network you see in the log. The “Always allowed IPs” take precedence."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1143
msgid "Referrer domains that are always blocked (403), one per line, e.g. copy-site.example:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1143
msgid "Requests that come from links or embeds on these sites. Each entry also covers its subdomains."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1144
msgid "Hide usernames from visitors"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1144
msgid "?author=1, 2, 3… returns “page not found” instead of the redirect to /author/username/, the REST API does not list users, the users sitemap is removed and oEmbed shows the site instead of the author. Logged-in users see everything as before. Author archives with a link stay."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1147
msgid "How much one visitor may read per minute, stricter limits for some visitors, countries, and the temporary block for those who keep going."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1148
msgid "Limits per IP"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1150
msgid "Pages per minute (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1150
msgid "Starting value: 60. Above the limit it returns 429. Be careful with networks that share an IP (companies, mobile carriers) and with CDNs: set the “Real visitor IP” correctly first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1151
msgid "Searches (?s=) per minute (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1151
msgid "Search is heavy for the server and a favourite of scrapers. Starting value: 20."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1152
msgid "REST API (/wp-json/) and GraphQL requests per minute (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1152
msgid "Only read requests from visitors. Cart, checkout and forms (POST) do not count. Starting value: 60."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1153
msgid "“Page not found” (404) per minute (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1153
msgid "Scrapers guess addresses (?p=1, 2, 3…, old product URLs) to find content. Missing images, CSS, scripts and the favicon do not count. Starting value: 30."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1154
msgid "Sitemaps per minute (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1154
msgid "Scrapers read the sitemap first to find every page. Covers the sitemaps of WordPress, Rank Math, Yoast and similar plugins. Google, Bing and the other verified search engines are never limited. Starting value: 5."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1155
msgid "IPv6: also limit the whole /56 network (four times the page limit)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1155
msgid "Pages are counted per /64, because one connection usually gets a whole /64. A server or a home connection often has a /56 or more, so a scraper can take a new /64 for every request. This also counts the /56 the /64 belongs to, up to four times the page limit (429 above it, without a block). Some mobile networks give neighbouring phones addresses of the same /56: on a site with many visitors from them, keep it off. Always on in Emergency Mode."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1156
msgid "Pages per minute from data centers (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1156
msgid "People rarely browse from a server; scrapers very often run on one. Visitors from the published addresses of AWS, Google Cloud, Oracle Cloud, DigitalOcean and Akamai / Linode get this stricter limit instead of the normal one. The lists are downloaded from the providers once a day. Some VPNs use these providers, so their users get this limit too: it is meant for reading, not for blocking. The always-allowed User-Agents (monitoring, price platforms) and verified search engines are not affected. Starting value: 15. 5 in Emergency Mode."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1157
msgid "Watch for attacks spread over many IPs (automatic Emergency Mode)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1157
msgid "The limits per IP cannot see a scraper that spreads its requests over hundreds of IPs. The whole site can: ScrapeLock learns how many pages per minute your site usually serves, and when that is exceeded five times over for 3 minutes in a row (and never below the minimum below), it does what you choose here. Verified search engines and exempt staff are not counted. Pages served from a page cache without reaching WordPress are not counted either."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1158
msgid "When it happens:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1163
msgid "Email me and show a notice with a “Start Emergency Mode” button (recommended)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1164
msgid "Start Emergency Mode for 1 hour on its own, and email me"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1166
msgid "A rush of real visitors (a newsletter, a link on a popular site) looks the same as an attack. Emergency Mode changes many settings at once, listed in its box on the first tab, e.g. excerpts instead of full text in lists and stricter limits for data centers, where some services in “Always allowed” run. Feeds stay open to feed readers and podcast apps."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1169
msgid "Minimum pages per minute for the automatic start:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1169
msgid "Below this the site is never considered under attack, however quiet it usually is. Starting value: 300 (5 pages per second)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1174
msgid "Stricter page limit for visitors who have not shown they are people"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1174
msgid "A small script waits for the visitor's first real interaction (scroll, tap, key or mouse movement), solves a light challenge in the background and receives a cookie for 7 days. Nobody sees a captcha or a window. Visitors without the cookie (scripts, and people with JavaScript turned off) get the limit below instead of the normal page limit. Search engines and verified AI search bots are not affected. It works with page caches such as WP Rocket. A determined scraper can repeat the steps, but each of its IPs has to do the work."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1175
msgid "Pages per minute without the cookie (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1175
msgid "Starting value: 20. A person reads far fewer pages per minute, and gets the cookie with the first scroll or tap."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1180
msgid "Download the free country database (DB-IP Lite, once a month)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1180
msgid "Needed when the site is not behind Cloudflare or Bunny CDN. About 5 MB to download, stored as two small files in uploads/scrapelock-geo. Behind Cloudflare the country that Cloudflare sends is used, behind Bunny the one Bunny sends (when it reaches the site directly from Bunny), and the database is not needed."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1181
msgid "Blocked countries (403), two-letter codes separated by commas, e.g. CN, RU:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1181
msgid "Search engines, verified AI search bots and the “Always allowed” list are never blocked by country. People who travel or use a VPN appear with the country of their connection."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1182
msgid "Countries with a stricter page limit, e.g. those your customers do not come from:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1183
msgid "Pages per minute for these countries (0 = off):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1183
msgid "Starting value: 10."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1189
msgid "Block after this many violations within 10 minutes (0 = never):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1189
msgid "Violation: every minute in which the IP exceeded a limit, and every fake Googlebot. The trap blocks immediately."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1190
msgid "Block duration (minutes):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1192
msgid "How long the log is kept is set on the Log tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1197
msgid "Network and CDN (advanced)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1200
msgid "Only for sites behind a CDN or a proxy, and for the checks that run before WordPress and the page cache. Most sites never need to change these."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1203
#: includes/class-pncp-health.php:439
msgid "Real visitor IP"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1210
msgid "REMOTE_ADDR (no CDN/proxy)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1216
msgid "Behind a CDN or reverse proxy all visitors appear with the CDN's IP. Choose the header with the real IP."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1219
msgid "Trusted Proxy:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1219
msgid "the header is read only when the request comes from a proxy you trust. Otherwise anyone could write any IP they want and bypass limits and blocks. CF-Connecting-IP: only from Cloudflare. X-Real-IP / X-Forwarded-For: from Bunny CDN, the server itself or a private network (Nginx in front of Apache). True-Client-IP: only from the proxies in the list."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1221
msgid "Trust Cloudflare addresses"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1221
msgid "The official Cloudflare list is refreshed every day."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1222
msgid "Trust Bunny CDN addresses"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1222
msgid "For X-Real-IP / X-Forwarded-For and Bunny's country header. The official list of Bunny edge servers is refreshed every day."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1225
msgid "Trust every request (1.4 behaviour, insecure)"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1225
msgid "On because this is how version 1.4 worked. Fill in your proxies below and uncheck it. Once turned off, it cannot be turned on again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1228
msgid "Other trusted proxies / load balancers (IP or CIDR, one per line):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1229
msgid "CDN shared secret (optional):"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1229
msgid "Only when \"Real visitor IP\" is a CDN header (CF-Connecting-IP, X-Real-IP, X-Forwarded-For). A CDN (Bunny, Cloudflare) is multi-tenant: its edge IPs are shared, so by default anyone could point their own CDN zone at your origin and set the real-IP header. Set a secret here and configure your CDN to send it on every request as the header “X-ScrapeLock-CDN”; the CDN’s real-IP header is then trusted only when the secret matches. Leave empty to keep the current behaviour. For best effect, also restrict your origin so it is reachable only through the CDN."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1230
msgid "Only through the CDN: refuse (403) requests that do not bring the secret"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1230
msgid "Someone who finds your server's own address can go around the CDN and everything it blocks. With this on, every request without the secret in the X-ScrapeLock-CDN header gets a 403, also pages from the page cache when the pre-cache check is on. First make the CDN add the header to every request: in Bunny CDN, an Edge Rule with the action “Set Request Header” (X-ScrapeLock-CDN = your secret) for all requests; in Cloudflare, Rules → Transform Rules → “Modify Request Header”, set static. It can only be turned on from a request that brings the secret, so you cannot lock yourself out by mistake. Not affected: the server itself (cron, cache preload), WP-CLI. Files the web server sends without WordPress (images, CSS, JS) are not covered. If the CDN ever stops sending the header, add define( 'SCRAPELOCK_CDN_ONLY', false ); to wp-config.php."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1232
msgid "This request brought the secret: the CDN sends it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1232
msgid "This request did not bring the secret: the CDN does not send it yet, or you opened the site around the CDN."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1235
msgid "Turned off in wp-config.php (SCRAPELOCK_CDN_ONLY)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1240
msgid "What the server sees on this request:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1247
msgid "Trusted proxy:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1247
msgid "yes"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1247
msgid "no"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1248
msgid "IP the plugin uses now:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1254
msgid "Early checks"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1257
msgid "Early check: block known bots before the theme and the other plugins load"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1257
msgid "Adds the small file wp-content/mu-plugins/scrapelock-early.php, which stops blocked IPs and referrers, temporarily blocked IPs and User-Agents in the bot list with less server load. Search engines, logged-in users, forms and feeds are left to the normal check. It is removed when you turn this off or deactivate the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1259
msgid "The file could not be created (the server does not allow direct file writes to wp-content/mu-plugins). The normal check works as before."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1262
msgid "Pre-cache check: apply the page limit and blocks also to pages served from the page cache"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1262
msgid "Page caches such as WP Rocket serve stored pages before any plugin loads, so a bot that looks like a browser could read them without a limit. This adds one line at the top of wp-config.php that loads a small check before the cache: always-blocked IPs, temporarily blocked IPs and the “Pages per minute” limit. Counters are kept in APCu or in a folder of the uploads directory (uploads/scrapelock). Search engines, logged-in users, forms, wp-admin and the REST API are left to the normal check. The line and the files are removed when you turn this off or deactivate the plugin."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1282
msgid "Blocking at the CDN (advanced)"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: CDN name, 2: number of addresses
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1286
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s: %2$s address blocked now"
msgid_plural "%1$s: %2$s addresses blocked now"
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: %d: requests per minute
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1287
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1321
#: includes/class-pncp-health.php:394
#: includes/class-pncp-health.php:413
msgid "Off"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1305
msgid "This part has its own button: it saves only the connection to the CDN, not the settings above."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1306
msgid "The IPs ScrapeLock blocks temporarily are also blocked by your CDN, with your own account. A scraper that keeps going is then stopped at the CDN, before its requests reach your server: no PHP, no database, no bandwidth. Each block is removed when the temporary block ends. Only the blocked addresses are sent, with the reason and the end time; nothing about your visitors or content."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1309
msgid "The site is locked: this setting cannot be changed until it is unlocked."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1312
msgid "Paused: the real visitor IP is read from a header without checking the proxy, so anyone could get any address blocked. Turn off “Trust every request” under “Real visitor IP” first."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1318
msgid "CDN"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1329
msgid "Zone ID"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1332
msgid "Cloudflare: the Zone ID on the Overview page of your site (32 characters). Bunny CDN: the ID of the Pull Zone that serves this site (a number, in the address of its page in the bunny.net dashboard)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1336
msgid "API token"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1339
msgid "Set in wp-config.php (SCRAPELOCK_EDGE_TOKEN)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1343
msgid "Cloudflare: create an API token (My Profile → API Tokens → Create Token → Custom token) with the single permission Zone → Firewall Services → Edit, for this zone only. Bunny CDN: the API key of your account (Account settings → API); it gives access to the whole account. The token is stored in the database and never shown again; to keep it out of the database, add define( 'SCRAPELOCK_EDGE_TOKEN', '…' ); to wp-config.php instead."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1348
msgid "Save and test the connection"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1359
msgid "Test blocking at the CDN"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1360
msgid "Blocks the address 203.0.113.x (reserved for documentation, it belongs to nobody) at the CDN, checks that the CDN lists it and removes it again. No setting changes and no visitor is affected."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: number of addresses, 2: CDN name
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1364
#, php-format
msgid "%1$s address blocked at %2$s now."
msgid_plural "%1$s addresses blocked at %2$s now."
msgstr[0] ""
msgstr[1] ""

#. translators: %s: date and time
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1367
#, php-format
msgid "Last update: %s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: date and time, 2: error message
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1371
#, php-format
msgid "Last error (%1$s): %2$s"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: list of IP addresses
#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1381
#, php-format
msgid "These blocks could not be removed at the CDN by ScrapeLock; remove them in the CDN dashboard: %s"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1384
msgid "Bunny CDN blocks single addresses: a blocked IPv6 network (/64) stays blocked by ScrapeLock only."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1386
msgid "Never blocked at the CDN: the IPs administrators used in the last 30 days (a block at the CDN also covers wp-admin), search engines, AI search services and the CDN's own servers."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-admin.php:1400
msgid "The site is behind Cloudflare, but all visitors appear with a Cloudflare address."
