msgid "The site was not locked: the guard file wp-content/mu-plugins/scrapelock-lockdown-guard.php could not be written, because WordPress cannot write files to that folder directly. Without it, someone who can change the database directly (for example through a vulnerable plugin) could unlock the site. Let the web server write to wp-content/mu-plugins (create the folder if it is missing), then lock again. Or tick \"Lock without the guard file (weaker)\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-lockdown.php:2507
msgid "The site was not unlocked: the guard file wp-content/mu-plugins/scrapelock-lockdown-guard.php could not be changed. Check that the web server may write to that folder, or unlock from the server with SCRAPELOCK_UNLOCK."
msgstr ""

