msgid "Too many wrong codes. Try again later."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-lockdown.php:2557
msgid "Important: there is only one way to unlock"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-lockdown.php:2559
msgid "Only the 6-digit code from the authenticator app on your phone unlocks the site. There is no reset by email or SMS, no \"forgot code\" link, and no other administrator, your hosting company or ScrapeLock support can unlock it from WordPress."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-lockdown.php:2560
msgid "Backup: the 10 recovery codes shown once when you connect the app. Print them and keep them away from the phone; each one unlocks the site once."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-lockdown.php:2561
msgid "Lost both the phone and the recovery codes? Only someone with access to the server files (FTP or your hosting panel) can unlock the site, by adding a line to wp-config.php."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-lockdown.php:2562
msgid "While locked, password resets for staff are frozen too: if you forget your WordPress password, the same line in wp-config.php is the way back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-lockdown.php:2564
msgid "The app is tied to the security keys in wp-config.php (AUTH_KEY, AUTH_SALT). Some security plugins and hosting companies change them automatically, for example after a scan: the app codes then stop working and only a recovery code or the wp-config.php line unlocks the site. To avoid this, add a key of ScrapeLock's own to wp-config.php BEFORE you connect the app:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-lockdown.php:2566
msgid "The app is tied to the security keys in wp-config.php (AUTH_KEY, AUTH_SALT), which some security plugins and hosting companies change automatically. To tie it to a key of ScrapeLock's own instead: first remove the app below, then add SCRAPELOCK_KEY to wp-config.php, then connect the app again. Adding the key while the app is connected makes its codes stop working."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-lockdown.php:2580
msgid "Multisite network"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-lockdown.php:2582
msgid "The lock covers the whole network: locking or unlocking here does it for every site."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of sites
#: includes/class-pncp-lockdown.php:2588
#, php-format
msgid "When you lock, ScrapeLock saves a signed copy of the plugins active on the whole network, the super admins, the network admin email and the registration setting, and of the protected settings and administrators of every site where ScrapeLock is active (up to %d sites). Each site checks its own copy and puts back what was changed directly in the database. An account made a super admin or a site administrator behind WordPress's back cannot sign in."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of sites
#: includes/class-pncp-lockdown.php:2599
#, php-format
msgid "The guard file keeps the plugins active on the whole network (with ScrapeLock) and, for the first %d sites, their active plugins and theme as they were when you locked, from the start of every request."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %d: number of sites
#: includes/class-pncp-lockdown.php:2610
#, php-format
msgid "Limits: sites added after you locked are not covered until you unlock and lock again. On a network with more than %d sites, the full copy of the settings of the other sites is saved on their first visit after you locked, from the values that still match the fingerprints taken when you locked: a setting changed directly in the database before that visit is reported, but apart from the active plugins and the theme it cannot be put back."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-pncp-lockdown.php:2620
msgid "This network was locked with an earlier version of ScrapeLock: only the site where it was locked has a saved copy of its settings, and the super admins and the network plugins are not checked. Unlock and lock again to protect every site."
msgstr ""

#. translators: 1: number of sites, 2: number of sites
#: includes/class-pncp-lockdown.php:2623
#, php-format
msgid "Sites covered by this lock: %1$d of %2$d (sites where ScrapeLock is not active are not counted as covered)."
msgstr ""

